[4m[1;34mPrimary documentation link[0m ([90mhttps://example.com/docs[0m)

[4m[1;34mA longer link label that wraps across lines in narrow viewports[0m
([90mhttps://example.com/docs/deck/mode/long/link[0m)

Link activation should not accidentally advance the deck. Focus should remain
usable on the current slide only.

[1;32m# [0m[1;32mImage Syntax[0m

![4m[1;34mTiny transparent pixel[0m ([90mdata:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAAAACw=[0m)

This exercises Markdown image output without requiring network access. The image
is intentionally tiny so it does not dominate the slide.

[1;32m# [0m[1;32mLong Word Pressure[0m

The renderer should avoid layout explosions from a long token:

[35msupercalifragilisticexpialidocious-supercalifragilisticexpialidocious-supercali…[0m

Normal prose after the long token should remain visible.

[1;32m# [0m[1;32mEscapes And Entity Text[0m

Escaped punctuation should remain readable as literal text: [35m*not emphasis*[0m,
[35m[not a link][0m, and [35m# not a heading[0m.

Entity-looking text should also remain readable: [35mAT&amp;T[0m, [35m&lt;tag&gt;[0m, and
[35m10&nbsp;000[0m.

[1;34m## [0m[1;34mSecond-Level Slide Header[0m

This slide starts with a [35m##[0m ATX heading instead of [35m#[0m. The deck renderer should
still treat it as the slide header and keep the body content below it.

[1;35m### [0m[1;35mThird-Level Slide Header[0m

This slide starts with a [35m###[0m ATX heading. It verifies that lower-level first
headings can act as slide headers without inheriting body centering behavior.

[1;32m# [0m[1;32mFinal Slide[0m

[1;34m## [0m[1;34mEnd State[0m

This slide verifies [35mEnd[0m, [35mG[0m, URL hash restoration, and slide number rendering
near the end of the deck.
